1	From aa598f71593c9295ce110c99dc73adda46bb18a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
2	From: oscartu <oscarmh.tu@moxa.com>
3	Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 13:17:39 +0800
4	Subject: [PATCH 2/2] [Plan E Task 3] ies-auto-mibs: forward at the
5	 local/remote boundary
6	
7	sysObjectID came back as ISS's generic .1.3.6.1.2.1 instead of the Moxa
8	product OID .1.3.6.1.4.1.8691.600.1.5.4: the entry carries
9	GENERATE_SYS_OID and is computed by snmpd itself, so ISS cannot serve
10	it. Same class as the synthesised-index regression fixed in 2ed5f03,
11	and it appeared at the same place in the same way - which is the point.
12	Enumerating flags at the top of mox_snmp_handle_entry() had already
13	failed once.
14	
15	The forwarding therefore no longer sits at the top of the GET path. It
16	now sits inside entry_handle_generate_iss_value_file() and
17	entry_handle_generate_uri_value_file(), in the else-branch of the local
18	value producer, immediately before the call that would leave the
19	process. Everything reachable before that point - the in-process
20	callbacks behind ChkEntryGetValue(), URI_FIXED_VALUE, GENERATE_SYS_OID
21	- is local by construction, so a local producer added later is not
22	forwarded without anyone having to remember a list.
23	
24	Both generators take reginfo/reqinfo/request and return the new
25	IES_GET_FORWARDED, on which the caller answers NOERROR and stops.
26	
27	SYNTHETIC_INDEX stays an explicit guard on the forward. It is local for
28	a different reason: the value does come from ISS, but the column only
29	exists after iss_snmp_makeup_index() has run locally, so no subagent can
30	serve it.
31	
32	Two side effects of moving the forward past the cache check:
33	  - unlink(fname) + util_table_snapshot_reset() now run before each
34	    forwarded GET. The unlink drops stale local value files, which is
35	    the safer direction; the reset can cost a redundant ISS read in a
36	    walk that mixes forwarded and local tables.
37	  - a table whose snapshot is still inside the 800 ms window is served
38	    from that snapshot instead of being forwarded. Only reachable after
39	    a local fallback has already happened, and it self-heals.
40	
41	ret in both generators was uninitialised on the paths that return
42	mox_snmp_flask_handle_result(..., ret); harmless before, but it could
43	now surface as a bogus IES_GET_FORWARDED. Initialised to IES_ERR.
44	
45	Host-gcc syntax check with the target's flags is clean. Cross-compile
46	and DUT verification are the operator's step.
47	
48	Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
49	Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PbNj6tYZPRSSva5V9kqGYL
